WEBVTT

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:27.150
<i>The year is 1890.</i>

00:01:27.650 --> 00:01:32.070
<i>Nadia and the others manage to make it to Africa after many adventures.</i>

00:01:32.360 --> 00:01:35.610
<i>Nadia met a boy and fell in love with him there.</i>

00:01:35.610 --> 00:01:39.450
<i>But she was disappointed in love, and left feeling crushed.</i>

00:01:39.620 --> 00:01:44.660
<i>Cheer up, Nadia! You have just a few stories left.</i>

00:01:57.010 --> 00:01:59.890
1, 2, 3, 4...

00:01:59.890 --> 00:02:02.470
5, 6, 7, 8...

00:02:05.930 --> 00:02:08.350
And he whispered to her,

00:02:08.350 --> 00:02:10.900
"The stars are not very clear tonight."

00:02:14.570 --> 00:02:18.990
So many things have happened since we've arrived in Africa.

00:02:18.990 --> 00:02:22.030
Yeah, Marie's no longer a child.

00:02:22.030 --> 00:02:25.330
I never thought I would meet Gonzalez in such a place.

00:02:25.330 --> 00:02:28.330
You've had so many experiences too, Miss Grandis.

00:02:29.250 --> 00:02:30.710
I guess.

00:02:31.170 --> 00:02:34.090
Hey, what is that?

00:02:34.090 --> 00:02:36.460
Oh, that's a giraffe.

00:02:36.460 --> 00:02:38.130
A giraffe?

00:02:38.130 --> 00:02:40.090
Yes, and those are hippopotami.

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:41.930
How big!

00:02:41.930 --> 00:02:44.760
You can see the African elephants there too.

00:02:47.680 --> 00:02:49.440
It's just like a zoo!

00:02:52.270 --> 00:02:54.440
A lion!

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:56.070
Lion?

00:02:56.820 --> 00:02:58.740
But it's different than King.

00:02:58.740 --> 00:03:02.030
Of course, King is just a baby now.

00:03:02.030 --> 00:03:04.200
He'll grow up to be like that.

00:03:10.830 --> 00:03:12.420
So funny!

00:03:12.420 --> 00:03:14.460
So uncool!

00:03:15.590 --> 00:03:18.170
I'm glad you're always happy, Marie.

00:03:22.970 --> 00:03:24.510
Nadia...

00:03:28.270 --> 00:03:32.600
Say, why is Nadia so blue lately?

00:03:32.600 --> 00:03:34.520
Perhaps she's sick?

00:03:34.520 --> 00:03:36.900
Idiot! She's lost a love.

00:03:36.900 --> 00:03:37.780
Lost a love?

00:03:37.780 --> 00:03:40.820
Yes, the worst condition in life.

00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:44.660
I see. Is Nadia going to be all right?

00:03:44.660 --> 00:03:47.950
Jean, you're too nice a guy.

00:03:51.330 --> 00:03:54.380
I feel sorry for you, Jean.

00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:59.550
To love Nadia, he must be ready for trouble.

00:03:59.880 --> 00:04:04.300
I didn't expect this much trouble though.

00:04:05.430 --> 00:04:10.140
Listen, Jean, do you know what it's like to love women?

00:04:10.140 --> 00:04:11.430
No.

00:04:11.430 --> 00:04:12.640
It's hell!

00:04:12.640 --> 00:04:13.810
Hell?

00:04:13.810 --> 00:04:15.400
Yes!

00:04:15.400 --> 00:04:21.240
Since the dawn of time, it's been very troublesome to love women.

00:04:21.240 --> 00:04:22.490
Really?

00:04:22.490 --> 00:04:26.620
Yes, teenage girls are better.

00:04:27.370 --> 00:04:31.000
They're satisfied with just their own love.

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:35.040
But grown women are no good!

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:37.420
Right, they ask for presents.

00:04:37.420 --> 00:04:38.670
And dates.

00:04:38.670 --> 00:04:40.880
And interesting places to visit.

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:42.670
And they want to be entertained.

00:04:42.670 --> 00:04:44.760
And don't make mistakes with their age.

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:47.390
And don't look at other women.

00:04:47.390 --> 00:04:49.760
And they want to eat delicious foods.

00:04:49.760 --> 00:04:52.810
And tell a funny joke sometimes.

00:04:52.810 --> 00:04:54.520
And take her out in a nice car.

00:04:54.520 --> 00:04:56.400
They ask so much.

00:04:56.400 --> 00:05:01.860
Men must satisfy their requests. They take advantage of our love.

00:05:01.860 --> 00:05:07.620
Only those who can bear that hell can become happy.

00:05:07.620 --> 00:05:10.160
That's right! I had plenty of my own problems back then.

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:11.660
Really?

00:05:11.660 --> 00:05:12.500
Really!

00:05:16.750 --> 00:05:19.130
It's important to seize the opportunity after all.

00:05:19.130 --> 00:05:24.260
Listen, Jean, love yields fruit when two people are aware of it.

00:05:24.760 --> 00:05:26.220
You can expect her love.

00:05:26.680 --> 00:05:29.680
You just don't have a chance now.

00:05:30.260 --> 00:05:32.390
What shall I do then?

00:05:32.640 --> 00:05:34.350
Figure it out by yourself.

00:05:36.140 --> 00:05:38.060
But just this time,

00:05:38.690 --> 00:05:41.360
I will give you some advice.

00:05:41.900 --> 00:05:42.820
What shall I do?

00:05:43.440 --> 00:05:44.280
Sing!

00:05:44.900 --> 00:05:45.610
Sing?

00:05:45.610 --> 00:05:48.570
Yes, singing is the best way to tempt women.

00:05:49.120 --> 00:05:52.290
Listen, Jean, this is your best chance!

00:05:52.290 --> 00:05:55.450
Write a song using all of your scientific technology

00:05:55.450 --> 00:05:58.420
and all of your love!

00:05:58.790 --> 00:06:01.840
Tell Nadia how you feel about her.

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:04.260
For example, something like this!

00:07:51.950 --> 00:07:54.120
A love song?

00:09:28.830 --> 00:09:30.880
Hey, will you read this book to me?

00:09:31.090 --> 00:09:32.510
Yeah, later.

00:09:32.510 --> 00:09:33.590
Later?

00:09:34.470 --> 00:09:35.550
Read it now!

00:09:36.220 --> 00:09:38.260
Sorry, but later, okay?

00:09:39.680 --> 00:09:41.180
Boring...

00:09:42.310 --> 00:09:42.600
Hearing those sweet words,

00:09:42.600 --> 00:09:44.600
Hey, please read this book.

00:09:44.980 --> 00:09:48.020
she felt her heart melt like jelly.

00:09:48.020 --> 00:09:50.560
And her lightly painted lips

00:09:50.560 --> 00:09:51.520
conveyed her passionate decision to him.

00:09:51.520 --> 00:09:52.940
Boring...

00:09:54.400 --> 00:09:56.280
Hey, please read this book!

00:09:57.740 --> 00:09:59.740
Hey! Hey!

00:10:00.830 --> 00:10:02.280
Boring...

00:10:03.660 --> 00:10:05.450
Hey, will you read this book to me?

00:10:05.910 --> 00:10:07.750
Later, okay?

00:10:09.420 --> 00:10:11.000
Boring...

00:10:12.250 --> 00:10:14.130
Hey, please read this book to me!

00:10:14.670 --> 00:10:16.840
Sorry, a little later!

00:10:17.760 --> 00:10:19.510
Boring...

00:10:20.590 --> 00:10:22.560
Hey, please read this book to me!

00:10:26.100 --> 00:10:27.560
Depressing...

00:10:31.810 --> 00:10:33.320
Boring...

00:12:37.560 --> 00:12:38.110
Jean...

00:12:41.400 --> 00:12:42.320
Hey, Jean!

00:12:43.030 --> 00:12:46.280
What is it, Nadia? What's wrong?

00:12:47.320 --> 00:12:48.530
Nothing at all!

00:12:48.530 --> 00:12:50.240
Nadia!

00:12:57.420 --> 00:13:00.500
What, what, what? That Jean!

00:13:00.500 --> 00:13:03.840
He's always, always, always thinking about his inventions!

00:13:03.840 --> 00:13:06.140
Why are you looking so down?

00:13:06.510 --> 00:13:08.010
Grandis!

00:13:09.390 --> 00:13:13.480
Are you feeling down because nobody understands your feelings?

00:13:14.440 --> 00:13:15.980
No, it's not like that.

00:13:15.980 --> 00:13:19.900
Then, are you lonely because nobody worries about you?

00:13:20.770 --> 00:13:22.400
Especially Jean.

00:13:22.400 --> 00:13:24.280
No, you're wrong!

00:13:25.030 --> 00:13:26.950
Well, never mind.

00:13:27.610 --> 00:13:31.700
You feel lonely because you need someone.

00:13:31.700 --> 00:13:34.410
That's a good thing for you.

00:13:34.910 --> 00:13:40.130
It's pretty attractive for charming girls to make fun of boys at times.

00:13:40.750 --> 00:13:43.550
But Jean is always so absorbed in his inventions.

00:13:43.550 --> 00:13:44.340
Nadia!

00:13:45.010 --> 00:13:49.640
Don't take advantage of his love. You don't know what he's doing.

00:13:50.720 --> 00:13:51.640
But...

00:13:51.970 --> 00:13:54.520
Man becomes most earnest

00:13:54.520 --> 00:13:57.480
when he's trying to do something for his love.

00:13:58.190 --> 00:14:00.190
Never forget that.

00:14:02.020 --> 00:14:04.900
I know that.

00:14:05.780 --> 00:14:07.490
Really?

00:14:07.490 --> 00:14:09.370
It'll be okay, then.

00:16:04.100 --> 00:16:06.730
I did it! It's perfect!

00:16:07.270 --> 00:16:08.690
The score is perfect too.

00:16:09.070 --> 00:16:10.690
Next is Nadia!

00:16:10.690 --> 00:16:12.030
What? A song?

00:16:12.030 --> 00:16:13.860
Yes, a song for you.

00:16:13.860 --> 00:16:15.740
I've written one just for you!

00:16:19.040 --> 00:16:20.450
What's this?

00:16:20.870 --> 00:16:22.920
An automatic ukulele.

00:16:23.250 --> 00:16:25.920
An automatic ukulele?

00:16:25.920 --> 00:16:32.720
Yes, I put this together with spare parts from the Gratan,

00:16:32.720 --> 00:16:34.640
and with modern scientific technology!

00:16:35.300 --> 00:16:38.010
All I have to do is sing the score.

00:16:38.010 --> 00:16:40.680
My voice goes through this microphone in sync with the music.

00:16:40.970 --> 00:16:43.940
You can hear it from this loudspeaker.

00:16:45.060 --> 00:16:47.940
It's amazing that you could make this in one day and a night.

00:16:48.270 --> 00:16:49.820
I did it for my love.

00:16:50.940 --> 00:16:54.570
Thank you, Jean. I'm so happy.

00:16:54.570 --> 00:16:57.320
You must listen to the song first.

00:16:57.320 --> 00:16:58.620
Okay...

00:16:58.620 --> 00:17:00.120
Right, let's go!

00:17:01.500 --> 00:17:02.960
Switch on!

00:19:50.580 --> 00:19:52.540
What is it, Nadia?

00:19:53.330 --> 00:19:54.790
That's enough.

00:19:57.590 --> 00:19:58.550
That was awful.

00:20:01.010 --> 00:20:03.890
Awful? Why?

00:20:04.550 --> 00:20:06.510
Sanson, you liar!

00:20:11.520 --> 00:20:12.690
Oh, dear.

00:20:12.690 --> 00:20:14.190
You can't win if you don't try.

00:20:14.190 --> 00:20:15.980
He took a chance.

00:20:15.980 --> 00:20:18.690
Have you ever taken a chance?

00:20:18.690 --> 00:20:21.240
I don't fight battles that I can't win.

00:20:27.160 --> 00:20:28.120
Nadia.

00:20:29.750 --> 00:20:31.200
Grandis...

00:20:36.460 --> 00:20:39.760
Do you dislike Jean?

00:20:40.630 --> 00:20:42.130
No.

00:20:42.420 --> 00:20:44.550
Then, you like him?

00:20:45.140 --> 00:20:46.850
Yeah, probably.

00:20:47.180 --> 00:20:49.600
Why did you do that then?

00:20:50.810 --> 00:20:51.850
I don't know.

00:20:53.350 --> 00:20:55.650
I guess it was just embarrassing.

00:20:56.520 --> 00:21:01.400
It's so painful and embarrassing that I can't be honest.

00:21:02.320 --> 00:21:03.990
I understand.

00:21:05.700 --> 00:21:10.370
Everyone has his own limits.

00:21:10.370 --> 00:21:16.330
To love someone means crossing those limits.

00:21:17.130 --> 00:21:19.880
It's natural that you became confused.

00:21:20.250 --> 00:21:26.680
But you can't live within your limits.

00:21:28.010 --> 00:21:33.770
You'll be able to eat meat and fish for him someday.

00:21:34.270 --> 00:21:36.230
I'm afraid.

00:21:36.230 --> 00:21:43.780
Don't worry. You'll be happy to be able to love someone.

00:21:44.950 --> 00:21:47.530
That's love.

00:21:48.410 --> 00:21:49.700
Really?

00:21:51.830 --> 00:21:52.700
Really.

00:21:53.790 --> 00:21:57.170
I see. This is love.
